G3824.def:
παλινγενεσία (Rec. παλιγγ-), -ας, ἡ 
(πάλιν, γενεσις), 
new birth, renewal, restoration, regeneration; 
__(a) of persons (Plut., Phil., al.), of spiritual regeneration, διὰ λουτροῦ παλινγενεστίας (genitive attr., see Ellic., in l), Tite 3:5; 
__(b) of the world, as in Stoics, Jewish Apocal., al. (see Dalman, Words, 177 ff.), Matthieu 19:28.†

G3835.def:
πανοῦργος, -ον 
[in LXX chiefly for עָרוּם ;] 
ready to do anything; 
__(a) in cl., chiefly in bad sense, knavish, crafty: 2 Corinthiens 12:16; 
__(b) in good sense, skilful, clever (Proverbes 13:1 28:2).†

G3843.def:
πάντως 
adv. (πάς), [in LXX: 4Ki.5:11 (see Thackeray, Gr., 47), Tob.14:8, al. ;] 
altogether, by all means; 
__(a) without neg. (from Hdt. on) : 1 Corinthiens 16:12; esp. in strong affirmations, surely, at all events: Luc 4:23, Actes 21:22 28:4, 1 Corinthiens 9:10; 
__(b) with neg. (so always in mom.), in a complete negation: Romains 3:9; in a partial negation (Bl., § 75, 7), 1 Corinthiens 5:10.†

G3858.def:
παρα-δέχομαι 
[in LXX: Exode 23:1 (נָשָׂא), Proverbes 3:12 (רָצָה), 2Ma.4:22 R, 3Ma.7:12 * ;] 
to receive, admit; 
__(a) of things: Marc 4:20, Actes 15:4 16:21 22:18, 1 Timothée 5:19; 
__(b) of persons: Hébreux 12:6 (LXX).†

G3877.def:
παρ-ακολουθέω, -ῶ 
[in LXX: 2Ma.8:11 2Mac 9:27 R* ;] 
with dative, to follow closely, accompany. Metaphorical, in various senses, 
__(a) to result: Marc 16:17; 
__(b) to follow up, trace, investigate: Luc 1:3 (so frequently in cl.); 
__(with) to follow as a standard of conduct: 1 Timothée 4:6, 2 Timothée 3:10. (For exx. from π., see MM, xviii.)†
